              "start": 0,
              "end": 125,
              "quote": "中国政府最近敲定了设立大熊猫国家公园的计划。大熊猫国家公园占地面积约为黄石国家公园的三倍，将成为我国首批国家公园之一。这项计划将把保护范围扩大到大量此前未受保护的区域，并把许多现有的大熊猫保护区归由同一个机构管理，以提高管理成效、减少管理上的不一致。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "zh:grammar-fill-2",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "grammar-fill-2"
              ],
              "start": 126,
              "end": 269,
              "quote": "经过三年的试点期，大熊猫国家公园将于明年正式设立。公园的设计旨在体现“保护自然生态系统的原真性和完整性，保护生物多样性，保护生态缓冲区，并为子孙后代留下宝贵的自然资产”这一指导原则。公园的主要目标是增强彼此隔离的大熊猫种群及其栖息地之间的连通性，并最终使野生大熊猫种群数量达到理想水平。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "zh:grammar-fill-3",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "grammar-fill-3"
              ],
              "start": 270,
              "end": 360,
              "quote": "大熊猫还充当着伞护物种，让中国西南和西北地区的众多动植物也得到保护。设立大熊猫国家公园，是为了给生活在大熊猫分布区内的所有物种提供更有力的保护，并显著改善该地区生态系统的健康状况。"
            }
          ]
        },
        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:grammar-fill-1",
            "paragraphId": "grammar-fill-1",
            "text": "The Chinese government recently finalized a plan to set up a Giant Panda National Park(GPNP). Covering an area about three times the size of Yellowstone National Park, the GPNP will be one of the first national parks in the country. The plan will extend protection to a significant number of areas that were previously unprotected, bringing many of the existing protected areas for giant pandas under one authority to increase effectiveness and reduce inconsistencies in management."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:grammar-fill-2",
            "paragraphId": "grammar-fill-2",
            "text": "After a three-year pilot period, the GPNP will be officially set up next year. The GPNP is designed to reflect the guiding principle of “protecting the authenticity and integrity(完整性)of natural ecosystems, preserving biological diversity, protecting ecological buffer zones, and leaving behind precious natural assets(资产)for future generations”. The GPNP’s main goal is to improve connectivity between separate populations and homes of giant pandas, and eventually achieve a desired level of population in the wild."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:grammar-fill-3",
            "paragraphId": "grammar-fill-3",
            "text": "Giant pandas also serve as an umbrella species(物种), bringing protection to a host of plants and animals in the southwestern and northwestern parts of China. The GPNP is intended to provide stronger protection for all the species that live within the Giant Panda Range and significantly improve the health of the ecosystem in the area."
          }
        ],
